PATCH A -- value_framework.py: fv_to_6yr_avg_war has no knot below FV 40, so it
returns ONE value for the whole 20-40 range. CORRECTNESS. Verified zero movement
at or above FV 40 (tools/_sweep_calib_patchcheck.py: 0 of 162 grade x side cells
moved; expected_surplus_usd unchanged everywhere, the FV<=40 dollar anchor owns
that region).
=============================================================================
--- a/value_framework.py
+++ b/value_framework.py
@@
 def fv_to_6yr_avg_war(fv: float | None) -> float | None:
-    """Monotone (piecewise-linear) interpolation of the config anchor mapping FV
-    to the six-year AVERAGE annual WAR. Clamps outside the anchor range."""
+    """Monotone (piecewise-linear) interpolation of the config anchor mapping FV
+    to the six-year AVERAGE annual WAR. Clamps ABOVE the anchor range; BELOW the
+    lowest knot it extends with the concave low-end curve `realized_implied_fv`
+    already uses, so the forward map and the inverse map agree there.
+
+    LOW-END EXTENSION (calibration sweep 2026-07-25, data/xfv_level_calibration_eval.json).
+    The fitted empirical anchors start at FV 40 (`anchor_calibration.tiers` has no
+    sub-40 entry), so the plain clamp returned ONE value for the entire 20-40
+    range: 88.3% of the served eFV board (data/xfv.json, 4477 active rows) and
+    every sub-40 farm member summed by farm_grade_backtest.py:165. Meanwhile
+    `realized_implied_fv` DOES resolve that range, re-spreading it as
+    fv = 20 + 25*(war/war45)**_LOWEND_FG_EXP, so the two halves of one contract
+    disagreed by up to 20 FV points (every grade in [20, 40] round-tripped back
+    to 39.8). Inverting that same curve and pinning it to the lowest anchor knot
+    makes them mutual inverses (round-trip error <= 0.20 FV) and changes NOTHING
+    at or above the lowest knot. Measured support: the DB cohort empirical_anchors
+    itself fits on has an FV-35 cell, n=386, at 0.040 WAR/yr (bootstrap CI95
+    [0.020, 0.061]) against the clamp's 0.19; the extension returns 0.100 there.
+    Cohort-weighted |anchor - empirical| over tiers <= 60 improves 0.1536 ->
+    0.1431 WAR/yr.
+    """
     if fv is None:
         return None
     try:
         f = float(fv)
     except (TypeError, ValueError):
         return None
     if not math.isfinite(f):
         return None
     # Prefer the EMPIRICAL anchors re-derived from resolved cohorts (continuous
     # calibration, written to the fit file by --fit); fall back to the config seed.
     cal = _config().get("anchor_calibration", {})
     fitted_anchors = (_fitted().get("empirical_anchors") or {}).get("anchors") if cal.get("use_empirical") else None
     anchor = fitted_anchors or _config()["fv_to_6yr_avg_war"]
     pts = sorted((float(k), float(v)) for k, v in anchor.items())
     if f <= pts[0][0]:
-        return pts[0][1]
+        x0, y0 = pts[0]
+        if f <= 20.0:
+            return 0.0                       # the 20-80 grade floor: no expected value
+        if x0 <= 20.0:
+            return y0                        # knot already at the floor: nothing to extend
+        return y0 * ((f - 20.0) / (x0 - 20.0)) ** (1.0 / _LOWEND_FG_EXP)
     if f >= pts[-1][0]:
         return pts[-1][1]

